#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:36
#: 593ef87866bf4c6496d76ee1eac98543
msgid "Connection and Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:42
#: 7e82ef5c051c477787a9f3b7a543f0ac
msgid "ESCs should be daisy chained together using CAN splitter boards and then one 4-pin CAN cable should be connected to the autopilot's CAN port.  Note that the last splitter board has a terminator (i.e. no port) on one side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:46
#: 68f2d27604644c61befa61cf3806690d
msgid "If using a Cube autopilot, the CAN1 and CAN2 labels are reversed.  These instructions assume the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port which is labelled \"CAN2\" on Cube autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:52
#: b234236552154872afc1e5787e569d90
msgid "Set the dip switches on each ESC to specify its unique number.  This number also maps the ESC to an equivalent PWM output on the back of the autopilot.  For example ESC 1 will react just like a normal PWM ESC connected to the autopilot's MAIN OUT 1.  By default this mapping also matches the :ref:`motor order diagrams <Copter:connect-escs-and-motors>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:53
#: 167619e934834e2ba5874bbeafff272b
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 3 (ToshibaCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:54
#: 11b2d055e21441db8bd32b676ba82020
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (First driver) to specify that the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:60
#: 17068988cdbb44ed901b8f0cd37c7236
msgid "Logging and Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:62
#: 1be47569840640f09515f0cf3de081aa
msgid "ToshibaCAN ESCs provide information back to the autopilot which is recorded in the autopilot's onboard log's ESCn messages and can be viewed in any :ref:`ArduPilot compatible log viewer <common-logs>`.  This information includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:64
#: 11273162f62449dc92df95f94e386ce8
msgid "RPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:65
#: 72ee09a1dff340ff83dd5efc085dcbbc
msgid "Voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:66
#: d55d7a4b7c8c4a24a269deef5beb9228
msgid "Current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:67
#: 78eeb2e79ce6422c8b0848b6a8b92b63
msgid "ESC Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:68
#: f510de33de9f4df5bbaaccadce11262b
msgid "Total Current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:69
#: 4c18513ea55c4160885f2a85fff959bf
msgid "Motor Temperature (if the optional motor temperature sensor is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:71
#: d82880ef464b4870a92ab66a08b6754f
msgid "The RCOU messages are also written to the onboard logs which hold the requested output level sent to the ESCs expressed as a number from 1000 (meaning stopped) to 2000 (meaning full output)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:73
#: cd21c02b793b41a29b3178d73031c15c
msgid "This information (except the motor temperature) can also be viewed in real-time using a ground station.  If using the Mission Planner go to the Flight Data screen's status tab and look for esc1_rpm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:81
#: 096710c856ea484aafdd2d9802a4d29a
msgid "Sending ESC data to the GCS requires using MAVLink2.  Please check the appropriate SERIALx_PROTOCOL parameter is 2 (where \"x\" is the serial port number used for the telemetry connection)."
msgstr ""
